{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 42,
  "title": "Passage 42",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s42-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p01.mp3",
      "en": "A red sky at sunset may mean that there are clear skies to the west, where the sun sets.",
      "cn": "日落时天空呈现红色，这可能意味着太阳落山的西方天空晴朗。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s42-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p02.mp3",
      "en": "A red sky at sunrise usually means that the clear weather has already passed, so storms might be coming.",
      "cn": "日出时天空呈现红色，则通常意味着晴天已经过去，所以暴风雨可能即将来临。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s42-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p03.mp3",
      "en": "Forecasting the weather has been practiced for thousands of years.",
      "cn": "预测天气已经被实践了数千年。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s42-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p04.mp3",
      "en": "In the 5th century BC, the Greeks sent out forecasts to sailors.",
      "cn": "公元前5世纪，希腊人就向航海者发布天气预报。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s42-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p05.mp3",
      "en": "They used signs in nature to forecast the weather.",
      "cn": "他们利用自然界的迹象来预测天气。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s42-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p06.mp3",
      "en": "But today, meteorologists provide exact forecasts further in advance.",
      "cn": "但如今，气象学家能够更提前地提供准确的天气预报。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s42-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p07.mp3",
      "en": "They use scientific instruments to study weather conditions around the world and make forecasts.",
      "cn": "他们使用科学仪器研究世界各地的天气状况，并进行预报。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s42-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p08.mp3",
      "en": "Pilots, farmers and many other people depend on these forecasts.",
      "cn": "飞行员、农民和其他许多人都依赖这些预报。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s42-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p09.mp3",
      "en": "Luckily, most of us can simply check the smartphone or turn on the TV to find out what kind of weather is coming.",
      "cn": "幸运的是，我们大多数人只需查看智能手机或打开电视，就能知道接下来是什么天气。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s42-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p10.mp3",
      "en": "If you are looking for some signs of the weather, pay attention to nature.",
      "cn": "如果你正在寻找一些天气的迹象，请关注大自然。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s42-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p11.mp3",
      "en": "There are two basic rules used in weather forecasting.",
      "cn": "天气预测中有两个基本规律。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s42-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p12.mp3",
      "en": "Weather generally moves from west to east.",
      "cn": "天气现象一般自西向东移动。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s42-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p13.mp3",
      "en": "And low air pressure usually means rain or snow.",
      "cn": "低气压通常意味着下雨或下雪。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s42-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p14.mp3",
      "en": "So pay attention to the signs.",
      "cn": "因此，要注意这些迹象。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s42-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p15.mp3",
      "en": "If rainbows form in the west at sunrise, the sun is on the way.",
      "cn": "如果日出时西边出现彩虹，那么晴天就在路上了。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s42-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p16.mp3",
      "en": "Smell the flowers, their smells are stronger in wet air.",
      "cn": "闻一闻花儿——在潮湿的空气中它们的香味更为浓郁。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s42-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p17.mp3",
      "en": "What are the ants doing?",
      "cn": "蚂蚁在做什么？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s42-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p18.mp3",
      "en": "Are they moving to higher ground?",
      "cn": "它们是否正往高处移动？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 19,
      "chunkId": "s42-p19",
      "image": "assets/images/19.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p19.mp3",
      "en": "This could mean a drop in air pressure.",
      "cn": "这可能意味着气压的下降。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 20,
      "chunkId": "s42-p20",
      "image": "assets/images/20.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p20.mp3",
      "en": "Are the birds flying low or high?",
      "cn": "鸟儿飞得是低还是高？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 21,
      "sourceSentenceId": 21,
      "chunkId": "s42-p21",
      "image": "assets/images/21.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p21.mp3",
      "en": "Falling air pressure may influence birds ears, so they fly low.",
      "cn": "气压下降可能会影响鸟儿的耳朵，所以它们会飞得低一些。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 22,
      "sourceSentenceId": 22,
      "chunkId": "s42-p22",
      "image": "assets/images/22.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p22.mp3",
      "en": "And if the sky is red at sunset, you might plan a picnic for the next day.",
      "cn": "如果日落时天空呈现红色，那么你就可以计划第二天的野餐了！"
    }
  ],
